# NestGlow Co — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development, and set the same names in Vercel's
# project settings for production. `.env.local` is gitignored; this file is not,
# so never put a real value in here.
#
# ⚠️ THIS CHANGED ON 2026-08-29. It used to say nothing here was required,
# because /api/lead forwarded to Formspree and Formspree needed no config.
# Formspree is GONE (see src/lib/sheet.ts for why), and the two LEAD_* values
# below are now MANDATORY:
#
#   Set     -> the lead is written to the Google Sheet. Normal operation.
#   Unset   -> /api/lead answers 500, the visitor sees the form's error state,
#              and the whole lead is written to the Vercel log so it can be
#              retyped. Nothing is silently swallowed, but nothing is recorded
#              either.
#
# RESEND_* and ZAPIER_* remain optional and additive: unset means that leg
# reports "skipped: …" and the lead still lands in the Sheet.

# ── Resend: the customer's confirmation email ────────────────────────────
# The receipt the CUSTOMER gets. NOT Caroline's copy of the lead — hers is the
# Sheet row plus the SMS. Resend is additive: with these unset,
# `sendConfirmation` returns "skipped: …", the lead is still recorded, and the
# skip is logged. A missing receipt is never an error the visitor sees.
#
# Free tier is 3,000 emails/month, far above anything this site will send.

# resend.com/api-keys. Sending permission only — it never needs to read.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# The From header, display name included:
#   NestGlow Co <hello@send.nestglowco.com>
#
# ⚠️ USE A SUBDOMAIN, NEVER THE ROOT DOMAIN. Resend needs its own SPF and DKIM
# records on whatever it sends from. Putting those on `nestglowco.com` itself
# would collide with the records carrying Caroline's own mailbox
# (nestglowco@gmail.com). The `send.` subdomain keeps the two senders out of
# each other's way. Same shape Gorsegner (send.gorsegnerbrothers.com, verified
# 2026-08-16) and BDF both use.
#
# ── WHERE THE DNS RECORDS GO ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hostinger's DNS Zone Editor, for now: nestglowco.com is still served by
# Hostinger and still points at the OLD site. Adding records for a `send.`
# subdomain does NOT require the site migration to happen first — the subdomain
# is independent of where the root domain points, so this can be set up before
# the DNS cutover and will survive it.
#
# After the cutover the zone may move; if it does, recreate these records
# wherever the zone then lives. Verify the domain in Resend BEFORE setting this
# value — an unverified domain returns a 403 and every receipt silently fails.
#
# Replies go to BUSINESS.email via reply_to, so a customer answering the receipt
# reaches Caroline rather than a no-reply address.
RESEND_FROM=


# ── Zapier: Caroline's SMS alert ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The "Catch Hook" URL from the Zap's trigger step. Looks like:
#   https://hooks.zapier.com/hooks/catch/1234567/abcdef/
#
# What it does: /api/lead POSTs one flat JSON object here the instant the
# contact form is submitted. The Zap texts it to Caroline via SMS by Zapier.
# Same pattern as Karla's quiz, without the Google Sheet in the middle, so there
# is no polling delay.
#
# It was WhatsApp first and that cannot work: Meta blocks marketing-category
# templates to US numbers while still returning success. See src/lib/zapier.ts.
#
# ⚠️ TREAT THIS AS A SECRET. It is unguessable, not authenticated — anyone
# holding the URL can push fake leads to Caroline's phone. Set it in Vercel as
# a normal (hidden) env var, not in config.ts.
#
# Additive, like Resend: unset means `notifyZapier` returns "skipped: …", the
# lead is still written to the Sheet, and the skip is logged. A missing text is
# never an error the visitor sees — but it does mean Caroline has not been told,
# so the route logs that one at error level.
#
# ⚠️ The Zap must be TURNED ON for this to do anything. An off or deleted Zap
# answers 410 and the log line reads `alert=FAILED: http 410` — that is the
# failure most likely to go unnoticed, because nothing visible breaks.
ZAPIER_LEAD_HOOK_URL=


# ── Google Sheet: THE RECORD OF EVERY LEAD (required) ────────────────────
# Replaced Formspree on 2026-08-29. `scripts/lead-intake.gs` is the source of
# what runs at the other end; its header comment has the full deploy procedure
# and the two mistakes that cost sessions on TCG.
#
# This is the one leg that can fail the visitor's submit. If the Sheet write
# fails, /api/lead answers 502 and the whole lead goes to the Vercel log,
# because with Formspree gone there is no second copy anywhere.

# The Apps Script web-app URL, ending in /exec. From the Sheet:
# Extensions → Apps Script → Deploy → Manage deployments → pencil → New version.
#
# ⚠️ Use the PENCIL, never "New deployment" — a new deployment mints a new URL
# and orphans this one. And change the Version dropdown to "New version", or it
# redeploys the previous snapshot to the same URL and reports success while
# serving your old code.
LEAD_SHEET_URL=

# A shared secret. The script compares it before writing anything, so without
# it anyone who found the /exec URL could append rows to Caroline's leads.
#
# Set the SAME value in two places or leads stop landing:
#   1. here / Vercel, as LEAD_WEBHOOK_TOKEN
#   2. Apps Script → Project Settings → Script Properties → LEAD_TOKEN
#
# ⚠️ A mismatch does NOT look like an error from the outside. Apps Script can
# only answer HTTP 200, so it returns `{ok:false,error:"unauthorized"}` with a
# 200 status. `deliver()` in src/lib/sheet.ts reads the BODY for exactly this
# reason — trusting the status code would turn every dropped lead into a
# thank-you screen.
#
# Any long random string works: openssl rand -hex 24
LEAD_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=
